    'An electrical circuit in a domestic house is protected by a $6\\text{ A}$ fuse and connected to the $240\\text{ V}$ mains. The appliances in Table 2.11 have power ratings: Bulb 1 ($100\\text{ W}$), Bulb 2 ($75\\text{ W}$), TV ($300\\text{ W}$), Heater ($1500\\text{ W}$), Iron ($900\\text{ W}$). List groups of these appliances that could be turned ON at the same time without blowing the fuse, and justify your answer.',
