    'Step 1: With the switch closed, $R_{\\text{eq}} = R + \\frac{R}{2} = 1.5R$; Bulb A gets full current $I = \\frac{V}{1.5R} = \\frac{2V}{3R}$, while B and C each get $\\frac{I}{2} = \\frac{V}{3R}$ (so A is brightest, $B = C$). Step 2: Opening the switch removes C, puts A and B in simple series ($R_{\\text{eq}} = 2R$), so current through A drops from $0.67\\frac{V}{R}$ to $0.50\\frac{V}{R}$ (A dims) while current through B rises from $0.33\\frac{V}{R}$ to $0.50\\frac{V}{R}$ (B brightens to match A).',
