    'Activity 3.7, 3.8 & 3.9',
    'Based on Activities 3.7, 3.8, and 3.9 (see Figures 3.32 & 3.35): (a) Describe the magnetic field pattern formed by iron filings around a bar magnet (Figure 3.32). (b) Where is the neutral point X located when two magnets are placed with like poles facing each other (Figure 3.35) or when a bar magnet is placed in the Earth\'s field? (c) In Activity 3.9 (magnetic shielding), why did inserting iron nails between the magnet and paperclips cause the paperclips to fall, whereas plastic drinking straws had no effect?',
