    'Step 1: Magnetic lines of force run from N to S outside the magnet (Figure 3.32) and never cross. Step 2: At a neutral point X (Figure 3.35), net magnetic flux density $B_{\\text{net}} = 0$. Step 3: Soft iron/ferromagnetic barriers redirect magnetic flux lines within their walls, creating magnetic shielding.',
